    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] It has been listed on the National Register of Historic Places since 1986.\n[2] As such, it is one of the largest areas of virgin tallgrass prairie in the state of Nebraska.\n[3] The first national tallgrass prairie ever designated in the U.S. and the largest conservation site in the Chicago Wilderness region, it is located on the site of the former Joliet Army Ammunition Plant between the towns of Elwood, Manhattan and Wilmington in northeastern Illinois.\n[4] Joliet Army Ammunition Plant (JOAAP, formerly known as the Joliet Arsenal) was a United States Army arsenal located in Will County, Illinois, near Elwood, Illinois, south of Joliet, Illinois.\n\nNotes:\n[verification] Nine Mile Prairie has been listed on the National Register of Historic Places since 1986."
